Id: lin039w
Severity: WARN
Category: packages
Check: deb_statoverride
Fix: chown and chmod as the detail gives, or change the override with dpkg-statoverride.
References: dpkg-statoverride(1)
Controls: CIS 3.3; NIST AC-3, CM-6; ISO 8.3; CE Secure configuration

A file's mode or owner differs from what dpkg-statoverride sets for it.
dpkg records no mode or owner for the files packages install, but it
keeps a list of overrides, which packages and administrators set for the
files whose mode matters: crontab and plocate setgid, the D-Bus launch
helper setuid to a group, /etc/ssl/private closed to all but ssl-cert.
'dpkg-statoverride --list' shows them, and dpkg applies them whenever
it installs or upgrades the package. A file that no longer matches has
been changed since: a setuid or setgid bit added or removed, or a group
that lets more people in. Entries whose file does not exist are not
reported.

To fix it, set the file back with the chown and chmod commands the
detail gives (chown first, since it clears the setuid and setgid bits).
If the new mode is what you want, change the override instead, so that
dpkg does not undo it at the next upgrade:

    dpkg-statoverride --remove /usr/bin/crontab
    dpkg-statoverride --update --add root crontab 2755 /usr/bin/crontab
